'''Loris''' is a city in [[Horry County, South Carolina]], United States. As of the [[2020 United States census|2020 census]], Loris had a population of 2,449.<ref name="Census2020PLLede">{{cite web|title=2020 Decennial Census Redistricting Data (Public Law 94-171)|url=https://api.census.gov/data/2020/dec/pl?get=NAME%2CP1_001N&for=place%3A42730&in=state%3A45|website=United States Census Bureau|year=2021|access-date=February 4, 2026|df=mdy}}</ref>
==History==
Loris was founded on December 7, 1887, as a [[Railway town|railroad town]], originally serving the [[Wilmington, Chadbourn and Conway Railroad|Wilmington, Chadbourn, and Conway Railroad]].<ref name="LCOC">{{Cite web |title=Loris Chamber of Commerce |url=https://lorischamber.com/history-of-loris#:~:text=By%201887,%20the%20rail%20line,names%20in%20the%20United%20States. |access-date=2024-10-14 |website=Loris Chamber of Commerce |language=en-US}}</ref> Loris was later incorporated on July 26, 1902.<ref name="LCOC"/> The first brick building, which housed the Bank of Loris, opened in 1907.<ref name="LCOC"/> Telephone lines to Conway were first used in 1909.<ref name="LCOC"/> The town grew steadily in the 1920s and 1930s; a high school opened in 1920, and by the 1930s, Loris had around 1,000 residents.<ref name="LCOC"/> In the 1970s, Loris legally became a city.<ref name="LCOC"/>

==Geography==
Loris is in northern Horry County on the [[Atlantic coastal plain]].

Highways include [[U.S. Route 701]], and [[South Carolina Highway 9#Loris business loop|SC Highway 9 Business]] (Main Street).

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city of Loris has a total area of {{convert|11.8|km2|order=flip}}, of which {{convert|0.05|km2|order=flip|2}}, or 0.43%, are water.<ref name="Census 2010">{{Cite web| url=https://factfinder.census.gov/bkmk/table/1.0/en/DEC/10_SF1/G001/1600000US4542730| title=Geographic Identifiers: 2010 Census Summary File 1 (G001): Loris city, South Carolina| publisher=U.S. Census Bureau| work=American Factfinder| accessdate=January 25, 2018| archive-url=https://archive.today/20200213100453/https://factfinder.census.gov/bkmk/table/1.0/en/DEC/10_SF1/G001/1600000US4542730| archive-date=February 13, 2020| url-status=dead}}</ref>

